#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_game_scores.html.heex:2
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Every match a registered, identified player finishes is written down. That covers matches against the computer and matches between two people in a P2P session. A guest's matches are played for fun and are not kept."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_game_scores.html.heex:34
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The result appears in your private conversation as a card with the score and a way into the game's channel. While you play, the P2P entry of the conversation shows which game. Rematch, on the result inside the session, offers the same game again."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_game_channels.html.heex:2
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Every Retro Game has its own channel, like %{channel}. The players of the game talk there, find partners and see the latest results. The channel %{feed} shows the results of every game."
msgstr ""

#: lib/retro_hex_chat_web/controllers/help_content/feature_game_scores.html.heex:19
